  </selectionEntries>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="b553467b-de41-58e8-b697-233e0c85b140" name="Epitome of Excess" hidden="false">
      <description>Infantry, Jump Infantry, Jet Pack Infantry, Beasts and Cavalry with this rule gain Fleet. Vehicles with this rule are Fast vehicles. If a model already has Fleet, its Run move is increased by 3". If a vehicle is already Fast, its Flat Out move is increased by 3". These bonuses do not stack with another instance of Epitome of Excess.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="fb0cdc24-b3ec-5060-b3eb-855bf3f83002" name="The Six-fold Path" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of each Shae'lait turn, every model with both Horror and The Six-fold Path uses the current game-turn step, maximum Step Six. Step 1: Feel No Pain (6+) and It Will Not Die (6+). Step 2: FNP (5+), IWND (6+). Step 3: FNP (5+), IWND (5+), +1 I. Step 4: as Step 3 plus Furious Charge. Step 5: FNP (4+), IWND (5+), +1 I, Furious Charge and improve invulnerable save by 1 (max 4+). Step 6: FNP (4+), IWND (4+), +1 I, Furious Charge, Rage and Daemon of Slaanesh; a model already with Daemon of Slaanesh gains Preferred Enemy (Aeldari) instead.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="4580ba87-c175-52a4-b6e6-4d0d5098c556" name="Seduction's Explicit Touch" hidden="false">
      <description>Whenever an enemy unit Falls Back because of a Morale, Fear or Pinning test directly caused by a unit containing this rule, roll an opposed Leadership test: 2D6 + highest Leadership in each relevant unit. If the Shae'lait wins, the enemy Falls Back a further D6" and may not Regroup until the start of its following turn. Fearless units are unaffected.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="cf741a93-7fad-538d-9d0d-9b7231f7eb68" name="From Horror and Unreality" hidden="false">
      <description>The unit has Daemonic Instability. If at least one natural 6 is rolled when resolving an Instability test and the unit survives, one model regains one lost Wound; until the next Shae'lait turn the unit counts its Six-fold Path as one step higher.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="48e6168d-3ecd-54a5-aa1c-fc43c902076a" name="Master's Bidding" hidden="false">
      <description>While a friendly Independent Character with the Shae'lait faction is joined to this unit, it gains Fearless and Implacable Advance. Look Out, Sir! rolls transferring a wound from that Character to a Horror model in the unit succeed on a 2+.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="6f8d577d-3b0e-5963-b691-c833bcc82093" name="Horror" hidden="false">
      <description>A Horror has Fear and is Tainted. A Tainted unit never counts as Scoring, though it may contest objectives. A Horror may not be the Warlord unless its entry specifically says otherwise.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="6fc24cfd-61de-53a9-9750-4e79f816dc26" name="Herd the Masses" hidden="false">
      <description>At the end of the Movement phase each enemy non-Fearless unit within 6" of one or more models with this rule takes one Leadership test. If failed it immediately Falls Back. A unit that passes is immune until the start of the next Shae'lait turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="23d15063-99a6-558c-b64b-69fdf333cd08" name="Seduction's Gaze" hidden="false">
      <description>Instead of firing one weapon, target a visible non-vehicle enemy unit within 12". Roll an opposed Initiative test using the highest Initiative in each unit. If the target loses, it is Initiative 1, may not Run and may not fire Overwatch until the start of the next Shae'lait turn. Models with no Initiative are unaffected.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="fad9b6b9-f79e-5a8c-b98a-3b17cc46bce6" name="Mark of Slaanesh" hidden="false">
      <description>The model adds +1 Initiative, maximum 10.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="53d221bf-47ca-5bdb-9442-fffb71b67561" name="Daemon of Slaanesh" hidden="false">
      <description>The model has Daemon, Fleet, Hatred (Daemons of Khorne) and Rending on melee attacks. Units entirely composed of these models add 3" to Run moves; Cavalry and Beasts instead add D6". Non-Walker vehicles add 3" to Flat Out moves.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="9bd388db-0626-5f00-9531-3036cf908408" name="Path of Excess" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of the Shae'lait Movement phase each Horror unit not within 12" of a friendly Shae'lait Character tests Leadership if an enemy Aeldari unit, enemy Character or enemy unit below half strength is within 18". If failed it becomes Ravenous until turn end: move toward nearest qualifying enemy by the shortest safe route, attempt to charge it if able, may not Go to Ground, and gains +1 Attack on a turn it successfully charges.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="4cc34fcd-77bd-5811-bb07-21aa70257165" name="Swiftstrike" hidden="false">
      <description>Attacks with this melee weapon are resolved at +2 Initiative, maximum 10. This cannot allow Unwieldy attacks above Initiative 1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="4a07d434-d29b-59ea-9b4a-c5e6f15b8e7f" name="Languid Strike" hidden="false">
      <description>The wielder suffers -1 Initiative for these attacks. At the start of each Fight sub-phase compare its modified Initiative with the average Initiative of enemy models in base contact; gain +1 Attack with this weapon per full point higher, maximum +3.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="991915d8-e8a4-58bd-84fb-3c0bfc6bf97d" name="Tendril Strikes" hidden="false">
      <description>The model does not use its Attacks characteristic with this weapon. Instead make 2D6 attacks, then add fixed bonus attacks for charging, Rage and similar rules. No bonus for two weapons.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="d6af2d96-58cc-5c42-8c5d-a9c4920d07fb" name="Neural Leak" hidden="false">
      <description>Always wounds non-vehicle models on a 4+ unless it would normally wound better. Each natural 6 To Wound gives the target unit -1 Initiative until end of next turn, minimum 1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="c01b771e-df30-5ab3-a30c-b9035f86c2cb" name="Impaled" hidden="false">
      <description>If a model suffers one or more unsaved Wounds from this weapon during a turn the wielder charged, that model is Initiative 1 for the remainder of the Assault phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="e0644f24-8e34-536e-97b8-8db54f5251bb" name="Bladestorm" hidden="false">
      <description>On a To Wound roll of 6 the attack is AP2 instead of its normal AP.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="5f0aacf6-edbb-5f78-93a6-a44149b8b89f" name="Rabble" hidden="false">
      <description>Before deployment, any number of Cultist Squads from the same platoon may combine into one unit. Mutant Rabble may combine only with other Mutant Rabble from that platoon. Once combined, they remain combined.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="e79d1c95-dcc3-5938-9850-c68e2cd6d76f" name="Be Useful Pawn" hidden="false">
      <description>While within 6" of a friendly model with Herd the Masses this unit gains Fearless. A friendly Shae'lait Character within 6" may make Look Out, Sir! rolls onto models in this unit on a 4+ even if not joined; a successful transfer kills one Cultist with no save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="96f32405-e303-5b2f-b0f5-019a87b62cdc" name="Mutant Overlords" hidden="false">
      <description>For each Exalted Cultist unit in the army, every Cultist Platoon Rabble may include one additional Mutant Rabble unit beyond its normal limit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8caef727-d353-595f-9087-0476457f361d" name="Glance of Power" hidden="false">
      <description>Whenever this unit rolls one or more natural 6s on To Hit, To Wound or saving rolls in a phase, improve its invulnerable save by 1 for the rest of that phase, maximum 4+.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="9e75f8ed-8d88-5cf0-9a29-742c6478c7fa" name="Lab-born" hidden="false">
      <description>If joined by a Flesh Crafter Focus Exalted, this unit gains Feel No Pain (6+) before applying the Six-fold Path; use the better value once the Path grants Feel No Pain.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="deb634e4-0adb-5a08-8885-550d4f3a9c78" name="Expendable" hidden="false">
      <description>Casualties from this unit never cause Morale tests for other friendly units and the unit never awards First Blood. It remains Scoring unless the mission says otherwise.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="20fd3c63-2e1a-50d0-9a0e-19d43202026d" name="Collar Discipline" hidden="false">
      <description>When this unit fails a Morale or Pinning test within 12" of a friendly Shae'lait Character or model with Herd the Masses, remove D3 Slaves to count the test as passed.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="17ebf470-8ba1-5057-bccd-98abaa4cd3a3" name="Blessed Perfection" hidden="false">
      <description>When the unit successfully manifests a psychic power and at least one Warp Charge die used was a natural 6, after resolving Perils roll a D6; on 5+ return one expended die to the Warp Charge pool, to a maximum of the dice originally rolled for that power.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="f33af17e-cb99-5f79-9692-969e52910694" name="Aura of Sedition" hidden="false">
      <description>Enemy models within 6" lose Stubborn and similar rules preventing Leadership modifiers. Fearless is unaffected.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1818cb7b-bf7e-5d29-81f4-48215cf14a29" name="Coiling Impact" hidden="false">
      <description>When the unit charges, each model inflicts one S5 Hammer of Wrath hit. A model suffering an unsaved Wound from these hits is Concussed for that Fight sub-phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="a7b90f09-92f7-5127-8b58-b3f644bd4d50" name="Carrion Feast" hidden="false">
      <description>At the end of any Assault phase in which an enemy unit was completely destroyed within 6", one Consumer regains one lost Wound. Maximum one Wound per phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="b4f2b414-5817-55db-a5d5-fdf3aeaf9750" name="Firstborn of the Shae'lait" hidden="false">
      <description>Friendly Horror units within 12" count their Six-fold Path as one step higher than normal. This does not stack with Master of Horrors.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="ec7b38f2-3f6f-5102-9f33-c69a818c1b1c" name="Gaze of the Firstborn" hidden="false">
      <description>Ezyrithn has Seduction's Gaze at 18" and may re-roll the opposed Initiative roll.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="a47f85f1-61ef-584d-a32a-6920d7e70015" name="Ancient Spite" hidden="false">
      <description>The model has Hatred (Aeldari).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="93e989e7-c92f-5e38-970b-82e94bed806c" name="Enraptorus Focus" hidden="false">
      <description>Gains Herd the Masses and Seduction's Gaze, carries an Ecstatic Shrieker, and enemy units within 6" suffer an additional -1 Leadership when testing because of Fear.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="62b5674d-d986-5987-ad97-96619a6ea701" name="Alchemist Focus" hidden="false">
      <description>Gains Poisoned (4+) on all non-vehicle Wounds inflicted by shooting and carries a Hallucinogenic Projector. At the start of each Shae'lait turn choose +1 Strength, Feel No Pain (6+) or Poisoned (5+); the Exalted and joined unit gain it until next turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="92c35c2d-3f14-5390-b42d-36479435e294" name="Summoner Focus" hidden="false">
      <description>Becomes Mastery Level 2 and generates from Slaanesh, Excess or Daemonology (Malefic). Once per battle a friendly Daemon unit Deep Striking within 6" does not scatter.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="25f3939f-dc3b-5296-b4b7-63d6bdf6daef" name="Flesh Crafter Focus" hidden="false">
      <description>Carries Apprentice Tools and a Flesh-stitcher Array. Once per Movement phase it may use the Array on a Horror within 6" instead of 3", succeeding on 3+.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="f1672f88-64f2-5820-af8f-5358afa78682" name="Six Sensations" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of each Shae'lait turn choose Avidity, Gluttony, Carnality, Paramountcy, Vainglory or Indolency. Until next turn gain respectively: Objective Secured; +1 Toughness; Seduction's Gaze; Herd the Masses; +1 WS and Attack; or Defensive Grenades and Concussive melee attacks. The same sensation cannot be chosen in consecutive turns.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="f42a2430-de53-584f-b39e-c410fc4ef19f" name="Feast Without End" hidden="false">
      <description>For every enemy model Beelzebothor slays in melee, roll a D6 after its attacks; each 6 restores one lost Wound. If it destroys a unit in melee it gains +1 Attack until the next Shae'lait turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8845a3e2-52c9-5e3d-aeca-a31ca678e7d9" name="Too Hungry to Command" hidden="false">
      <description>Beelzebothor may never be the Warlord despite being a Character.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="06cd7b83-6c45-5a07-9e98-8e0e7ee878c7" name="Unreality Made Flesh" hidden="false">
      <description>The first successful Hit scored against Aeos in each phase is discarded before To Wound/Armour Penetration. No effect against Stomp or Destroyer attacks.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="ede83b96-45bf-5ebb-a911-f044443dcbba" name="Mirrorstep" hidden="false">
      <description>In the Assault phase Aeos may make a 2D6" Thrust move instead of charging. If he does, he may not join or leave a unit during that move.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1b393c5a-a4ca-5038-84d4-8e15c61eca9b" name="Warp-slick Silhouette" hidden="false">
      <description>The Fighter has a 5+ invulnerable save against shooting attacks. If it Jinks, improve its cover save by 1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="e512c931-eb1f-59eb-b4ec-1f9fda940413" name="Doom of Culture" hidden="false">
      <description>Each time Karakiethal destroys an Aeldari unit, choose one Lesser or Moderate Broken Perfection effect it does not already have; it gains that effect for the rest of the battle. Character-only effects apply to Karakiethal.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="bad0174d-5f70-58a1-81b9-89202b594d95" name="Sixfold Crown" hidden="false">
      <description>Karakiethal's Six-fold Path is always one step higher than the normal game turn. At Step Six, instead of gaining Daemon of Slaanesh again, it gains +1 Attack.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="a2bf19e6-78ae-5aa2-afee-8704190c7275" name="Warp Veil" hidden="false">
      <description>The Centaur Titan has a 5+ invulnerable save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="d86d7c3a-5cee-500a-9353-a167b4dddc9f" name="Agile" hidden="false">
      <description>The Centaur Titan may choose a 4+ cover save against shooting until its next turn; if it does, it may fire only one primary weapon in its next Shooting phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="bd6a051d-727a-5269-a35a-3dec9ebca7d4" name="Webway Translation Engine" hidden="false">
      <description>If purchased, the Titan may begin in Reserve and arrive by Deep Strike. If it scatters onto impassable terrain or another model, reduce scatter by the minimum distance needed to place it legally instead of rolling a Mishap.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="2b80bef8-9bec-5dfb-a085-673bab484674" name="Covetous Claim" hidden="false">
      <description>If Thessyr ends your turn within 3" of an objective and no enemy Super-heavy or Gargantuan Creature is also within 3", he counts as controlling it. The first time each battle he scores VP from an objective, gain +1 additional VP.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="a640e522-edff-52b5-9f23-0c48fffe981b" name="Bottomless Feast" hidden="false">
      <description>Each time Gorathyl destroys a model in melee, roll D6; on 6 regain one Wound. If he destroys a unit, gain +1 Strength until end of next Shae'lait turn, maximum 10.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="5c5543d8-4c5d-5c15-88f1-33167f259e93" name="Perfect Enrapture" hidden="false">
      <description>Enemy units within 12" suffer -2 Leadership for Fear and Pinning. Enemy Characters in a Challenge with Ilyssae test Leadership at start of each Fight sub-phase or halve Attacks, rounding up.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="38e5d44d-d8c1-58ab-8b34-f73800e8b8b6" name="Crown Above All" hidden="false">
      <description>Friendly Shae'lait units within 12" gain Stubborn. Friendly Horrors within 12" ignore Path of Excess while Vaelithrax lives. Enemy units within 6" suffer -2 Leadership.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="9caaff5e-1c5a-5cae-9b5e-eeba9d40576c" name="Mirror of Triumph" hidden="false">
      <description>Whenever Saeloria wins a Challenge or your army gains a VP while she is locked in combat, gain +1 WS and +1 Attack until end of next Shae'lait turn, maximum +3 each. If she ends a turn without fighting or scoring while any enemy remains, she suffers Blind until next turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="80a173bc-a622-5880-8982-e460568c8ad8" name="Stillness Eternal" hidden="false">
      <description>Enemy units within 12" may not Run. Enemy units within 6" count as moving through Difficult Terrain and suffer -2 Initiative. Units already Initiative 1 also gain Slow and Purposeful.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="ab04398b-8a3e-5889-b510-27ab395f6a92" name="Seeker Blades" hidden="false">
      <description>Each Seeker Chariot inflicts D3 S4 AP- Rending Hammer of Wrath hits in addition to normal Chariot Hammer of Wrath.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="4fc95f97-caf9-5d03-89bf-74e65f60bcff" name="Hellflayer" hidden="false">
      <description>If a Hellflayer inflicts one or more unsaved Hammer of Wrath Wounds, its crew gain +D3 Attacks for that Fight sub-phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="0472ba56-b4e9-5ba2-ae00-aa89ada80149" name="Exalted Canopy" hidden="false">
      <description>An Exalted Seeker Chariot has a 5+ invulnerable save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="349974b9-f7a8-5153-977b-3bc706bd32dd" name="Bladevanes" hidden="false">
      <description>If the vehicle moves over an enemy unit during a Flat Out move, that unit suffers D3 S4 AP- Rending hits. A unit can be affected only once per turn by Bladevanes.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="27d9c501-4e9c-509a-8fd1-27a1866a1c1e" name="Trophy Chains" hidden="false">
      <description>Enemy units Tank Shocked by the Raider suffer -1 Leadership for the resulting Morale test.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="404c127c-3443-5249-becd-71017064b046" name="Scything Prow" hidden="false">
      <description>When Tank Shocking or Ramming, the Barge counts Front Armour as 14 and adds +1 Strength to any Ram hit, maximum 10.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="6787fe53-21f7-52b4-a963-5988ecbca208" name="Dais — Avidity" hidden="false">
      <description>A friendly Character embarked on the Dais counts as being within 3" of any objective the Dais itself is within 3" of for scoring purposes.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="69e56417-e6ce-5677-a758-09ab5ef67ad9" name="Dais — Gluttony" hidden="false">
      <description>The Dais gains It Will Not Die (5+).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="7f0cc2dd-52c3-5c50-88b4-a181398f7bb4" name="Dais — Carnality" hidden="false">
      <description>The Dais projects Seduction's Gaze from its hull using Initiative 6.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="e79c91fd-2f30-54c1-a5fa-fbc18382a7d8" name="Dais — Paramountcy" hidden="false">
      <description>Enemy units within 6" suffer -1 Leadership for Morale, Fear and Pinning tests.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="7580934c-fd72-58e1-b78c-e8f10a176063" name="Dais — Vainglory" hidden="false">
      <description>After the Dais destroys an enemy vehicle or causes an enemy unit to Fall Back, it gains +1 BS until end of next turn, maximum BS6.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8c27f715-5892-58af-811b-473dc56c8cef" name="Dais — Indolency" hidden="false">
      <description>Enemy units within 6" may not Run or fire Overwatch.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="3582c7e0-dcdc-515b-866f-5509d8dcb67d" name="From the Lab" hidden="false">
      <description>In From Raw and Rips, every Cultist Platoon Rabble, Exalted Cultist and Horrors from the Lab unit may select one Lesser Broken Perfection trait for free.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="2261d739-0492-55a5-9317-8c42a7c1bb86" name="From the Palace" hidden="false">
      <description>In From Raw and Rips, every Perfected Creations and Focused Shae'lait Exalted unit that purchases at least one Broken Perfection trait may select one additional trait of the same tier for free, obeying no-duplicate restrictions.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="739967a7-d53f-540c-a538-4466a9b6c1f9" name="Immaculate Pleasure" hidden="false">
      <description>At battle end, each enemy unit Falling Back that suffered fewer than 25% casualties awards +1 VP, maximum once per enemy unit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="86a8c615-4950-572b-bfc4-fa5de7747625" name="Unrestrained Host" hidden="false">
      <description>If the army contains three or more Horror units, at the start of each Shae'lait turn after the first choose one Horror unit not within 12" of a friendly Shae'lait Character. It automatically becomes Ravenous under Path of Excess without a Leadership test.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="389b4be6-d2f5-583f-aff5-9389ec94cb7b" name="Traitor Allegiance" hidden="false">
      <description>A Shae'lait detachment is always Traitor-aligned for Age of Darkness missions.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="bcd0aec6-c898-5aa0-a5e4-d76281d35323" name="Shae'lait Allies" hidden="false">
      <description>Sworn Brothers: Emperor's Children, Chaos Daemons, Daemons of the Ruinstorm. Fellow Warriors: other Traitor Legiones Astartes, Traitor/Dark Mechanicum, Traitor Imperialis Militia &amp; Cults. Distrusted: Traitor Solar Auxilia and other mortal Traitor forces not listed above. By the Emperor's Command: Loyalist Imperial forces and Aeldari. Narrative scenarios may override.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1797bd46-9047-5912-a954-a2e98d2a4c5e" name="Lord of War 25% Limit" hidden="false">
      <description>A Lord of War selected in this army is subject to the normal Age of Darkness 25% points limit. BattleScribe enforces the one-slot maximum here; compare the Lord of War subtotal to the roster total for the percentage limit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8ab4306a-d10f-5f6a-89c7-b144a4493548" name="From Raw and Rips Validation" hidden="false">
      <description>At least one HQ must have the Shae'lait faction and may not be a Horror. This catalogue enforces that requirement using the hidden Shae'lait Master category. Free From the Lab/From the Palace traits are presented as specifically labelled options and are valid only in this detachment.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="58505a0f-f880-5a94-99b0-c6e86bf74760" name="Fleet" hidden="false">
      <description>Use the standard Horus Heresy First Edition / Warhammer 40,000 7th Edition rule of this name. This local reference exists so the Shae'lait catalogue keeps the rule associated with the relevant unit or wargear without depending on a second catalogue's internal ID.</description>
    </rule>
