      <description>Use the standard Horus Heresy First Edition / Warhammer 40,000 7th Edition rule of this name. This local reference exists so the Shae'lait catalogue keeps the rule associated with the relevant unit or wargear without depending on a second catalogue's internal ID.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="614c49ea-3bcc-51ae-9743-79ab87c2dfa7" name="Soul Blaze" hidden="false">
      <description>Use the standard Horus Heresy First Edition / Warhammer 40,000 7th Edition rule of this name. This local reference exists so the Shae'lait catalogue keeps the rule associated with the relevant unit or wargear without depending on a second catalogue's internal ID.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="7c816b66-f9a4-58b5-a05f-f898eacb6ff8" name="One Use Only" hidden="false">
      <description>Use the standard Horus Heresy First Edition / Warhammer 40,000 7th Edition rule of this name. This local reference exists so the Shae'lait catalogue keeps the rule associated with the relevant unit or wargear without depending on a second catalogue's internal ID.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="40f0a974-c892-58c9-a94b-1b996e061aff" name="Vector Dancer" hidden="false">
      <description>Use the standard Horus Heresy First Edition / Warhammer 40,000 7th Edition rule of this name. This local reference exists so the Shae'lait catalogue keeps the rule associated with the relevant unit or wargear without depending on a second catalogue's internal ID.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="90038689-1e06-510e-bf84-a7f631e58abc" name="Open-topped" hidden="false">
      <description>Use the standard Horus Heresy First Edition / Warhammer 40,000 7th Edition rule of this name. This local reference exists so the Shae'lait catalogue keeps the rule associated with the relevant unit or wargear without depending on a second catalogue's internal ID.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="64cc0a70-634c-5388-beb8-6dcbc3d1aae3" name="Fast Skimmer" hidden="false">
      <description>Use the standard Horus Heresy First Edition / Warhammer 40,000 7th Edition rule of this name. This local reference exists so the Shae'lait catalogue keeps the rule associated with the relevant unit or wargear without depending on a second catalogue's internal ID.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="d39e5771-b497-5a60-8c14-96ff5c6289de" name="Chariot" hidden="false">
      <description>Use the standard Horus Heresy First Edition / Warhammer 40,000 7th Edition rule of this name. This local reference exists so the Shae'lait catalogue keeps the rule associated with the relevant unit or wargear without depending on a second catalogue's internal ID.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="48a1c2a0-83cd-5954-a4ed-ca92793b5d4b" name="Flying Monstrous Creature" hidden="false">
      <description>Use the standard Horus Heresy First Edition / Warhammer 40,000 7th Edition rule of this name. This local reference exists so the Shae'lait catalogue keeps the rule associated with the relevant unit or wargear without depending on a second catalogue's internal ID.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="3caea19b-1e91-52ef-b4ad-9ca882e0e2e2" name="Gargantuan Creature" hidden="false">
      <description>Use the standard Horus Heresy First Edition / Warhammer 40,000 7th Edition rule of this name. This local reference exists so the Shae'lait catalogue keeps the rule associated with the relevant unit or wargear without depending on a second catalogue's internal ID.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="05cea608-9548-5f8f-8c6b-82e9f557e8d6" name="Very Bulky" hidden="false">
      <description>Use the standard Horus Heresy First Edition / Warhammer 40,000 7th Edition rule of this name. This local reference exists so the Shae'lait catalogue keeps the rule associated with the relevant unit or wargear without depending on a second catalogue's internal ID.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="69b4376b-ec8a-5fb4-9569-85c574e0000a" name="Bulky" hidden="false">
      <description>Use the standard Horus Heresy First Edition / Warhammer 40,000 7th Edition rule of this name. This local reference exists so the Shae'lait catalogue keeps the rule associated with the relevant unit or wargear without depending on a second catalogue's internal ID.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="ecdaea77-cbec-502a-b3ff-a066c4aca22c" name="Objective Secured" hidden="false">
      <description>Use the standard Horus Heresy First Edition / Warhammer 40,000 7th Edition rule of this name. This local reference exists so the Shae'lait catalogue keeps the rule associated with the relevant unit or wargear without depending on a second catalogue's internal ID.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="e73c6935-38d7-5129-a80a-aff481688668" name="Unbound Stride" hidden="false">
      <description>All models gain Crusader.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="62ae5a02-58f5-557b-9ee4-377543f961b8" name="Ancient Spite — Broken Perfection" hidden="false">
      <description>The unit Character gains Hatred (Aeldari) and Preferred Enemy (Aeldari).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="520e2e92-7cef-5e95-b1f0-b21b553303c2" name="Whispered Formula" hidden="false">
      <description>If the unit contains a Psyker, that Psyker generates one additional power from Slaanesh or Excess. This does not increase Mastery Level.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="cbb2039a-f9a4-5f2d-968c-945af24c6117" name="Pain Remembered" hidden="false">
      <description>Models with Horror may re-roll Feel No Pain rolls of 1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="56c253a9-7088-5256-978d-7ba23c186138" name="Bone Shards" hidden="false">
      <description>All models gain Bone Shards: 6", S User, AP5, Pistol, Rending.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="4eb93288-7167-5b59-ba97-343f40e068cd" name="Opened Mind" hidden="false">
      <description>The unit Character becomes Mastery Level 1 and knows either Sensory Overload or Lash of Slaanesh Primaris. If already a Psyker, +1 Mastery Level to max 2.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="9564e7cf-0881-5ad0-96ec-d43293a87694" name="Perfect Aim" hidden="false">
      <description>All models gain Precision Strikes and Precision Shots.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="9828b9ce-ae74-54a0-a756-f872c54e516e" name="Boon of Avidity" hidden="false">
      <description>If the unit Character personally destroys an enemy unit whose starting cost was at least its base cost, gain +1 VP. Once per battle per Character.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="719bdf49-f146-5a77-a5d8-1d6264be9838" name="Boon of Gluttony" hidden="false">
      <description>At start of Fight sub-phase before attacks, the Character may forfeit up to three Attacks; for each, on 4+ regain one lost Wound up to starting value.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="667e2e43-03dd-5a2b-98a6-2c565e2896dd" name="Hatred Made Flesh" hidden="false">
      <description>All models gain Hatred (Aeldari) and Preferred Enemy (Aeldari).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="bf137a6e-0b1f-51fc-b4f6-ebecf9ce7070" name="Boon of Carnality" hidden="false">
      <description>At start of a Challenge the opposing Character tests Leadership; if failed halve Attacks rounding up and it cannot benefit from Counter-attack or Rage for that Fight sub-phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="24b29c34-f9ff-5bed-850c-e73a2c2eb34f" name="Rending Limbs" hidden="false">
      <description>All non-Unwieldy melee weapons gain Rending. Weapons already with Rending instead re-roll To Wound rolls of 1 in melee.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="fb30ef4f-25a1-5909-81a9-cb12ddbcf393" name="Crushing Arrival" hidden="false">
      <description>All models gain Hammer of Wrath; models already with it inflict D3 Hammer of Wrath hits instead of one.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="a9a10324-cff1-516a-99fa-dd6ec79b996d" name="Boon of Paramountcy" hidden="false">
      <description>If the Character can end Movement controlling/contesting an objective without moving farther from nearest enemy, it must. First time it personally controls an objective when VP are awarded, +1 VP.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8fea0958-5e38-546c-b769-8a3e21931467" name="Boon of Vainglory" hidden="false">
      <description>Each time your army gains one or more VP, roll D6: 4+ gives +1 WS, I and A until start next turn, max +2 total; 1-3 gives Blind until start next turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="a02dbdee-9440-5cac-9782-0370f5e6a531" name="Boon of Indolency" hidden="false">
      <description>Whenever the Character inflicts unsaved melee Wounds on a model, that model tests Leadership after its attacks. Fail: Concussed, I1, cannot Run/Overwatch until end next turn. If already affected by this boon, suffers Instant Death; Eternal Warrior reduces to one additional unsaveable Wound.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="bd9be4cf-46d7-5af9-a5b3-71a5548d527a" name="Boon of Magic" hidden="false">
      <description>Character becomes ML2 and generates Slaanesh/Excess; if already a Psyker, +1 ML max3 and generates one additional Slaanesh/Excess power.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="95325fe2-294f-5c50-9f48-7c8ac15b5b3f" name="Transfigured of the Sixth Circle" hidden="false">
      <description>Character gains Daemon of Slaanesh, Rampage and +2 I max10. If already Daemon of Slaanesh, gains Eternal Warrior instead while retaining Rampage and +2 I.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="d4d66ff2-7055-5978-839d-8445f84cba59" name="1 — Appetite Unbound" hidden="false">
      <description>Each time the Warlord destroys an enemy unit, it gains +1 Attack until the start of your next turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="5ce0b959-c5da-5477-be0a-10cd642a0fc1" name="2 — Instrument of Terror" hidden="false">
      <description>Enemy units within 12" suffer -1 Leadership for Morale, Fear and Pinning. Stacks with Soul Siphon of Paramountcy to a maximum total penalty of -3.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="2d545951-dd45-5ffb-9c9b-233533f9da22" name="3 — Impossible Grace" hidden="false">
      <description>The Warlord and its unit add +2" to Run and Charge moves and may re-roll failed Dangerous Terrain tests.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="db152071-cb8e-5da9-b833-c6c1dee500b8" name="4 — Master of Horrors" hidden="false">
      <description>Friendly Horror units within 6" count the Six-fold Path as one step higher. Does not stack with another Master of Horrors.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="57d7b606-4b9f-5472-8934-a1b65473690f" name="5 — Flesh is Merely Material" hidden="false">
      <description>The Warlord gains It Will Not Die (5+). Once per turn, after it regains a Wound from IWND, a friendly Horror within 3" may also regain one lost Wound.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="045ecdb1-3da1-5040-8842-90e38bc03884" name="6 — Scorn of the First Empire" hidden="false">
      <description>The Warlord gains Hatred (Aeldari) and Preferred Enemy (Aeldari). Against an Aeldari Warlord it also gains Precision Strikes.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="95d5bcc9-b05e-5056-8ba5-29d8cf86eb5c" name="Lash of Slaanesh (WC1)" hidden="false">
      <description>Primaris, Witchfire, 18". S4 AP3 Assault D6, Pinning. If target fails Pinning, it also suffers -1 Initiative until start of your next turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="a0d4b328-f814-5ec3-9acb-074d1c54b693" name="Sensory Overload (WC1)" hidden="false">
      <description>Malediction, 18". Target suffers Blind, -2 Initiative and may not fire Overwatch until start of your next Psychic phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="427661a1-8e74-5615-bca1-70b62d3ffd1d" name="Ecstatic Agony (WC1)" hidden="false">
      <description>Focused Witchfire, 12". Target model takes a Toughness test; if failed it suffers one Wound with Fleshbane and no armour or cover saves. Natural 6 on test causes no effect.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="94c3a6f4-ea40-5d3c-9f44-48a8017b8100" name="Siren's Call (WC1)" hidden="false">
      <description>Malediction, 18". Target immediately moves D6" toward Psyker by shortest safe route if able and may not Run in its next Movement phase. Vehicles unaffected.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="2b06da11-43f1-53c5-879a-86eb1f9c60b5" name="Perfected Reflex (WC1)" hidden="false">
      <description>Blessing. Psyker and unit gain +2 Initiative, Counter-attack and Hit &amp; Run until start of next Psychic phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="71924ac0-a527-5501-9a01-16513ad5b74f" name="Symphony of Pain (WC2)" hidden="false">
      <description>Nova, 9". Enemy units in range suffer -1 WS, -1 BS, -1 Initiative and gain Fear until start of next Psychic phase. Fearless ignores only Fear.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8b3eb588-1303-5880-a1b6-4e6d8edd8961" name="Kiss of the Dark Prince (WC2)" hidden="false">
      <description>Focused Witchfire, 12". Opposed Leadership test. If Psyker wins, target suffers D3 AP2 Wounds with Fleshbane; a To Wound roll of 6 has Instant Death.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="b902a584-074a-52a5-b60f-b30e93916570" name="Feast on Sensation (WC1)" hidden="false">
      <description>Excess Primaris, Blessing. Until next Psychic phase, whenever Psyker's unit destroys an enemy unit in Shooting or Assault, one model in Psyker's unit regains one lost Wound; max one per model per phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="bd9ff891-6d2d-569b-bdc1-ebf888e9f825" name="Avidity's Reach (WC1)" hidden="false">
      <description>Blessing, 12". One friendly unit gains Objective Secured until next Psychic phase. Horrors remain Tainted and cannot benefit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="2f371a66-e5b7-5d6f-ace8-14ce180500f9" name="Gluttonous Renewal (WC1)" hidden="false">
      <description>Blessing. Psyker immediately regains D3 lost Wounds; excess above starting value is lost.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="0069f955-b7ad-517b-822f-0deacda8c41a" name="Carnal Mirage (WC1)" hidden="false">
      <description>Malediction, 18". Target suffers -2 Leadership for Morale, Fear and Pinning and may not fire Overwatch until next Psychic phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="67fa3cde-e6e2-591b-b7ad-e867c8aeba38" name="Paramount Will (WC2)" hidden="false">
      <description>Malediction, 18". Target tests Leadership on 3D6 discarding lowest. If failed it may not voluntarily move farther from Psyker during next Movement phase and may not Sweeping Advance.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="82f262f7-410b-585c-ad31-566bbd066e3f" name="Vainglorious Ascension (WC2)" hidden="false">
      <description>Blessing. Psyker gains +1 WS, +1 S and +1 Attack and melee weapons gain Rending until next Psychic phase. If Psychic test contains two or more natural 6s, resolve Perils normally even if another rule would prevent it.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="66870757-ba33-5f1f-9458-7e8cc631875b" name="Indolent Oblivion (WC2)" hidden="false">
      <description>Malediction, 24". Target has Slow and Purposeful, Initiative 1, treats all terrain as Difficult until next Psychic phase and may not Run. Vehicles instead treat all terrain as Dangerous and may not Flat Out.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1cd0a97a-3c3e-5261-9053-73099178e2b4" name="Psychoactive Crown" hidden="false">
      <description>Confers a 4+ invulnerable save. Ezyrithn and his unit add +1 to Deny the Witch against Runes of Fate, Runes of Battle or Telepathy.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="446f12f5-e16d-549b-9cc2-e3cdca14c07e" name="Sensory Veil" hidden="false">
      <description>Defensive Grenades; gains Stealth until the bearer has fired a weapon or charged in the current turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="965df6f3-501e-54c0-a97f-764a5c91fc85" name="Icon of Slaanesh" hidden="false">
      <description>Friendly non-Daemon, non-Horror units within 6" gain Stubborn and Fleet. Multiple Icons do not stack.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="1d853ef3-2c67-5799-b3b3-633baf8d949c" name="Phantasm Mask" hidden="false">
      <description>Bearer has Fear. Enemy Characters in a Challenge with bearer suffer -1 Leadership.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="fe7ace63-5f38-5ed5-81f4-d96d7266eed4" name="Clonefield" hidden="false">
      <description>At start of each Challenge roll D3; reduce enemy Character's Attacks by this amount for that Fight sub-phase, minimum 1.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="0b3a6d18-f662-5e2a-97e3-2136dac6265e" name="Flesh-stitcher Array" hidden="false">
      <description>At end of Movement phase, attempt to restore one Wound to bearer or friendly Horror within 3"; 4+ restores one. A model may be targeted by only one Array per turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="d870ec8e-4af6-554f-bcab-d5a7748b05c5" name="Shimmerfield" hidden="false">
      <description>Bearer gains 5+ invulnerable save, or improves existing invulnerable save by 1 to max 4+.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="3ca081a1-9344-533f-ba4a-710a0668c08a" name="Webway Breach Node" hidden="false">
      <description>One use. At start of friendly Movement phase place marker in base contact. Friendly Shae'lait Infantry, Beast or Daemon units Deep Striking within 6" do not scatter that turn. Remove marker at end of phase.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="21ea84f5-d70e-5121-a15d-8f7680c9c0f5" name="Soul Siphon" hidden="false">
      <description>Independent Characters only. Base +20 points and +1 Wound; purchase exactly one Circle aspect.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8c9f88ec-8817-5ce4-8030-5217d23d04d8" name="Soul Siphon — Avidity" hidden="false">
      <description>Once per battle, immediately after bearer personally scores one or more VP, gain +1 additional VP.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="5d4bc631-19f6-500a-884b-98511ac1e238" name="Soul Siphon — Gluttony" hidden="false">
      <description>Bearer gains +1 Toughness, maximum 6.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="254011fe-d47f-5945-89a4-8ccb0442a7d8" name="Soul Siphon — Carnality" hidden="false">
      <description>Bearer gains Seduction's Gaze. If already has it, range becomes 18" and may re-roll opposed Initiative roll.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="4c9056cf-cb8a-5b53-8ca6-80e12500a409" name="Soul Siphon — Paramountcy" hidden="false">
      <description>Enemy units within 6" suffer -2 Leadership for Morale, Fear, Pinning and Regroup tests. Fearless unaffected.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="5d9cebeb-fcae-5805-ab85-04980d271309" name="Soul Siphon — Vainglory" hidden="false">
      <description>Whenever bearer wins a Challenge, gains +1 Attack for rest of battle, maximum +2, and gains Fearless while it has at least one such bonus.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="ec21d6b8-dc02-570d-9948-fa3b21c0d2b0" name="Soul Siphon — Indolency" hidden="false">
      <description>Bearer's melee attacks gain Blind and Concussive. A model suffering an unsaved Wound from them may not Run or fire Overwatch until end of its next turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="c374bbd9-0092-5e34-9497-582e7d24a2c2" name="Apprentice Tools" hidden="false">
      <description>Carries Manipulator Talon, pair of Mandible Scythes and Gout Spewer, and gains +1 Attack.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="9ddde174-a6fc-5595-91d0-6e5e543ba369" name="Exalted Shimmerfield" hidden="false">
      <description>Confers a 4+ invulnerable save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="00da1bb0-ee0c-57aa-b612-555a3d10acf4" name="Flickerfield" hidden="false">
      <description>Confers a 5+ invulnerable save.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="f64c57f4-1b17-567f-894b-f4ef4dd9d701" name="Enhanced Aethersails" hidden="false">
      <description>Use the standard Dark Eldar/Drukhari Enhanced Aethersails rule appropriate to the 7th Edition rules environment.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="bdc38520-f57b-5d08-a453-cec69a9411d0" name="Shock Prow" hidden="false">
      <description>Use the standard Dark Eldar/Drukhari Shock Prow rule appropriate to the 7th Edition rules environment.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="296f2f7b-98a5-58b9-82f3-113342174b48" name="Wings" hidden="false">
      <description>The Sensation of Perfection becomes a Flying Monstrous Creature.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="2806c3f1-887a-5e2c-a47c-76389bc0ae75" name="Mastery Level 1" hidden="false">
      <description>The model/unit is a Mastery Level 1 Psyker and follows the listed discipline access.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="47e701f9-e717-5e9c-89c3-33d4836decaa" name="Mastery Level 2" hidden="false">
      <description>The model/unit is a Mastery Level 2 Psyker and follows the listed discipline access.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="df8848f8-bc67-5489-befa-6075df581a6e" name="Mastery Level 3" hidden="false">
      <description>The model/unit is a Mastery Level 3 Psyker and follows the listed discipline access.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="94af624e-257d-59c2-8993-15aec6637931" name="Razorform" hidden="false">
      <description>+1 Initiative and +1 Attack; armour save becomes 5+.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="b5498141-1de8-5ba6-9622-74ec270f6bbd" name="Lureform" hidden="false">
      <description>Gains Seduction's Gaze and Hit &amp; Run.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="93b39b55-a296-5aed-b9b7-76955d024020" name="Bastionform" hidden="false">
      <description>+1 Toughness, Slow and Purposeful; Perfected Claws become AP2 but Unwieldy.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="4a406225-84e7-5f0f-92ba-e3f244928dc4" name="Vessel of Perfection" hidden="false">
      <description>The model gains +1 Attack and a Soul Siphon; the selected Circle aspect is included in the +25 point upgrade.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="7ba1cad3-be92-5a40-a45b-b888ed982571" name="Favoured Prefect" hidden="false">
      <description>Uses the Favoured Prefect profile (A2). The source supplies this profile without an explicit upgrade sentence; the BattleScribe implementation treats one Prefect as a free optional unit leader.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="880bd11f-461e-5a04-a30e-3a5f8ce486d0" name="Transport Eligibility — Daemonettes" hidden="false">
      <description>Trophy Venom: only if 6 models or fewer. Pleasure Raider: only if 12 or fewer. Tantalus Barge: only if 24 or fewer. Maximum one dedicated transport.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="34d98139-c89a-5118-be4d-175a1b07e30e" name="Additional Crew" hidden="false">
      <description>A Character on a Seeker, Hellflayer or Exalted Seeker Chariot may purchase two Exalted Daemonette crew for +60 points, plus one additional crew for +30 per Hull Point above 2. Each carries Lash of Despair or Excruciator Pike. Crew attacks use WS6 S4 I6 A2 and do not add separate Wounds.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="568c62dc-0606-519c-9c91-8caea448132e" name="Circle Sovereign Limit" hidden="false">
      <description>Each Circle Sovereign is Unique. An army may include no more than one Circle Sovereign. Normal Lord of War slot limits also apply.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="7809cbc9-dd37-595a-af79-97e3fe36f33d" name="Seeker of Slaanesh" hidden="false">
      <description>Independent Character becomes Cavalry and gains +1 Attack.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="48d8f50d-dcd6-55ad-95cd-a633199de6d3" name="Heartseeker Steed" hidden="false">
      <description>Independent Character becomes Cavalry and gains +1 Toughness, +1 Wound and +1 Attack; Toughness bonus does not alter Instant Death thresholds using unmodified Toughness.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="aa7c2d28-71dc-5199-bf96-4249bc71dea5" name="Transport Capacity — Trophy Venom" hidden="false">
      <description>Transport Capacity: 6 models. Bulky models count as 2; Very Bulky may not embark.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8f2fe7bd-5349-5212-8e45-c526668785a6" name="Transport Capacity — Pleasure Raider" hidden="false">
      <description>Transport Capacity: 12 models.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="ce7769f6-4f33-5ded-b514-541a30f7c71d" name="Transport Capacity — Tantalus Barge" hidden="false">
      <description>Transport Capacity: 24 models.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="a7670761-4e0e-5595-a5e4-db891bbb5f92" name="Transport Capacity — Dais of a Circle" hidden="false">
      <description>Transport Capacity: 6 models.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="eb6d2fe0-accb-5342-8ba2-619d139853c1" name="Discipline of Slaanesh" hidden="false">
      <description>Discipline of Slaanesh: Lash of Slaanesh (WC1): Primaris, Witchfire, 18". S4 AP3 Assault D6, Pinning. If target fails Pinning, it also suffers -1 Initiative until start of your next turn. | Sensory Overload (WC1): Malediction, 18". Target suffers Blind, -2 Initiative and may not fire Overwatch until start of your next Psychic phase. | Ecstatic Agony (WC1): Focused Witchfire, 12". Target model takes a Toughness test; if failed it suffers one Wound with Fleshbane and no armour or cover saves. Natural 6 on test causes no effect. | Siren's Call (WC1): Malediction, 18". Target immediately moves D6" toward Psyker by shortest safe route if able and may not Run in its next Movement phase. Vehicles unaffected. | Perfected Reflex (WC1): Blessing. Psyker and unit gain +2 Initiative, Counter-attack and Hit &amp; Run until start of next Psychic phase. | Symphony of Pain (WC2): Nova, 9". Enemy units in range suffer -1 WS, -1 BS, -1 Initiative and gain Fear until start of next Psychic phase. Fearless ignores only Fear. | Kiss of the Dark Prince (WC2): Focused Witchfire, 12". Opposed Leadership test. If Psyker wins, target suffers D3 AP2 Wounds with Fleshbane; a To Wound roll of 6 has Instant Death.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="986ed0ba-f63b-5640-b915-9bc14162841d" name="Discipline of Excess" hidden="false">
      <description>Discipline of Excess: Feast on Sensation (WC1): Excess Primaris, Blessing. Until next Psychic phase, whenever Psyker's unit destroys an enemy unit in Shooting or Assault, one model in Psyker's unit regains one lost Wound; max one per model per phase. | Avidity's Reach (WC1): Blessing, 12". One friendly unit gains Objective Secured until next Psychic phase. Horrors remain Tainted and cannot benefit. | Gluttonous Renewal (WC1): Blessing. Psyker immediately regains D3 lost Wounds; excess above starting value is lost. | Carnal Mirage (WC1): Malediction, 18". Target suffers -2 Leadership for Morale, Fear and Pinning and may not fire Overwatch until next Psychic phase. | Paramount Will (WC2): Malediction, 18". Target tests Leadership on 3D6 discarding lowest. If failed it may not voluntarily move farther from Psyker during next Movement phase and may not Sweeping Advance. | Vainglorious Ascension (WC2): Blessing. Psyker gains +1 WS, +1 S and +1 Attack and melee weapons gain Rending until next Psychic phase. If Psychic test contains two or more natural 6s, resolve Perils normally even if another rule would prevent it. | Indolent Oblivion (WC2): Malediction, 24". Target has Slow and Purposeful, Initiative 1, treats all terrain as Difficult until next Psychic phase and may not Run. Vehicles instead treat all terrain as Dangerous and may not Flat Out.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
